<header><p class="st-kicker">other · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Dominion of New Zealand</h1><p class="st-meta">1907 CE – 1947 CE · capital Wellington</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">New Zealand's four decades as a British dominion, which built one of the world's first welfare states and fought in both world wars.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> declined to join the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia">Commonwealth of Australia</a> in 1901. At the request of Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-ward">Joseph Ward</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-new-zealand">Colony of New Zealand</a> was proclaimed a dominion on 26 September 1907, signalling self-governing status within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a>. The change was largely symbolic, as the country already ran its own affairs.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-massey">William Massey's</a> Reform government held office from 1912 to 1925 and sent the expeditionary force whose losses at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli-campaign">Gallipoli</a> in 1915 shaped national identity. Farm exports of wool, meat and butter to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> dominated the economy, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Depression</a> hit hard. The first Labour government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-joseph-savage">Michael Joseph Savage</a>, from 1935, built state housing and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-security-act-1938">Social Security Act</a> of 1938. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-fraser">Peter Fraser</a> led the country through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> was cautious about formal independence and did not adopt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statute-of-westminster-1931">Statute of Westminster</a> of 1931 until November 1947. With that act it became fully sovereign, and the term dominion fell out of use.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dominion-of-new-zealand.jpg" alt="Dominion of New Zealand" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Original: Albert Hastings Markham Vector: Zscout370, Hugh Jass, s. File history · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Zealand.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1907 CE – 1947 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Wellington</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William Massey, Michael Joseph Savage, Peter Fraser</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism, Presbyterianism, Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Māori</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/new-zealand">New Zealand</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>New Zealand (dominion)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1927&amp;focus=dominion-of-new-zealand" aria-label="Dominion of New Zealand on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8948 3650 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dominion of New Zealand lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M9268 3906L293 2949M9268 3906L295 2949M9268 3906L706 3218M9268 3906L9384 3761M9268 3906L4997 651M9268 3906L9268 3906"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M293 2949h0M295 2949h0M706 3218h0M9384 3761h0M4997 651h0M9268 3906h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M9268 3906h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M9268 3906h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Wellington. <a href="/atlas?year=1927&amp;focus=dominion-of-new-zealand">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
